# =============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS — Agrovesto/infrastructure
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-
#       security/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# HOW TO READ THIS FILE
#   * Order matters. The LAST matching pattern wins, so the broad `*` rule goes
#     first and the specific ones below override it.
#   * Owners are GitHub teams, not individuals, on purpose: this repository
#     outlives any one person's access, and a team can be re-staffed without a
#     commit here. The teams referenced below all exist in the Agrovesto org and
#     all have members.
#
# ⚠️  PREREQUISITE — NOT YET DONE (verified 2026-09-24)
#   None of these teams has been granted access to this repository. A team only
#   becomes an effective code owner once it has `write` permission here; until
#   then GitHub renders these owners as unable to approve, and this file requests
#   reviews from people who cannot give them.
#
#   Check the current state with:
#       gh api /orgs/Agrovesto/teams/<team>/repos/Agrovesto/infrastructure
#   (a 404 means "not associated", which is what every team returns today)
#
#   Grant it with:
#       gh api -X PUT /orgs/Agrovesto/teams/infrastructure/repos/Agrovesto/infrastructure \
#         -f permission=push
#       # repeat for team-leads, and for backend/frontend if their rules below
#       # are uncommented
#
#   ⚠️  Do NOT turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection
#   until that is done. Combined with the missing permissions it makes the
#   repository unmergeable: the required reviewer would be a team that cannot
#   approve. Today nothing is enforced, so merging still works normally.
#
# ENFORCING IT
#   Listing owners here only *requests* their review. To make it a merge gate,
#   turn on "Require a pull request before merging" + "Require review from Code
#   Owners" in branch protection for the branches that matter:
#       main     -> prod/ and monitoring/ apply on merge here
#       dev      -> dev/ applies on merge here
#       devops   -> the working branch this repository is cut from
#   Until that is on, nothing below blocks a merge, and a self-merge stays
#   possible. That is deliberate for now: with two people on the infrastructure
#   team, a hard code-owner gate on every path would block the team on itself.
#   See docs/team.md for the review expectations that apply either way.
# =============================================================================

# --- Default ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything not matched below belongs to the infrastructure team.
*                               @Agrovesto/infrastructure

# --- Account bootstrap and identity -------------------------------------------
# One-time, account-wide, and hard to undo: the state bucket, the GitHub OIDC
# provider and the role that CI assumes to deploy with. A mistake here is not a
# bad plan, it is a pipeline that can no longer reach the account — or one that
# can reach more of it than intended.
/bootstrap/                     @Agrovesto/infrastructure @Agrovesto/team-leads
**/iam.tf                       @Agrovesto/infrastructure @Agrovesto/team-leads
**/trust-policy.json            @Agrovesto/infrastructure @Agrovesto/team-leads

# --- CI/CD --------------------------------------------------------------------
# These workflows hold OIDC credentials that can apply infrastructure. A change
# to a trigger, an environment or a secret name is a change to what runs with
# deploy rights, so it gets the same review as the IAM above.
/.github/workflows/             @Agrovesto/infrastructure @Agrovesto/team-leads
/workflows/                     @Agrovesto/infrastructure @Agrovesto/team-leads

# --- Production ---------------------------------------------------------------
# prod/ applies on merge to main and talks to live money-path resources: the
# ALB, RDS SQL Server, the ECS services and the authoritative DNS zone for
# nomaos.com. Several of these were ADOPTED from a pre-existing account (see
# docs/import-runbook.md), which means an attribute marked ForceNew does not
# produce a plan to review — it produces a replacement of a live resource.
/prod/                          @Agrovesto/infrastructure @Agrovesto/team-leads

# --- Monitoring ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Runs in the prod account but is non-critical infrastructure: losing it loses
# visibility, not traffic. Infrastructure team only.
/monitoring/                    @Agrovesto/infrastructure

# --- Dev ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# A disposable, scheduled, single-EC2 environment. Infrastructure team only.
/dev/                           @Agrovesto/infrastructure

# --- Cost and scan configuration ----------------------------------------------
# The budgets, the Checkov/Trivy suppressions and the coverage gates. Changing a
# suppression or a threshold is how a real finding gets quietly closed, so these
# are reviewed like policy rather than like configuration.
**/checkov.yml                  @Agrovesto/infrastructure @Agrovesto/team-leads
**/.trivyignore.yaml            @Agrovesto/infrastructure @Agrovesto/team-leads
/infracost.yml                  @Agrovesto/infrastructure @Agrovesto/team-leads
/infracost-usage/               @Agrovesto/infrastructure @Agrovesto/team-leads
/scripts/                       @Agrovesto/infrastructure

# --- Documentation ------------------------------------------------------------
/docs/                          @Agrovesto/infrastructure
/README.md                      @Agrovesto/infrastructure

